# Adobe Artifactory (npm) — supplemental notes
#
# Root `.npmrc` in this repo sets `@pim:registry` only (no secrets — commit-safe).
# Put tokens in your user ~/.npmrc using Artifactory "Set me up", never in this file.
#
# Official writable repo (from Artifactory UI):
#   https://artifactory-uw2.adobeitc.com/artifactory/api/npm/npm-adobe-release/
#
# Scoped auth (user ~/.npmrc), per Artifactory — replace SCOPE and use your token:
# @<SCOPE>:registry=https://artifactory-uw2.adobeitc.com/artifactory/api/npm/npm-adobe-release/
# //artifactory-uw2.adobeitc.com/artifactory/api/npm/npm-adobe-release/:_authToken=<token>
# //artifactory-uw2.adobeitc.com/artifactory/api/npm/npm-adobe-release/:email=you@adobe.com
# //artifactory-uw2.adobeitc.com/artifactory/api/npm/npm-adobe-release/:always-auth=true
#
# Or use: npm login --registry=... --auth-type=web --scope=@pim
#
# Unscoped `ado-pim` uses publishConfig.registry in packages/cli/package.json.
#
# Other read mirrors (if your doc uses them for installs only):
# https://artifactory-uw2.adobeitc.com/artifactory/api/npm/npmjs/
# https://artifactory.corp.adobe.com/artifactory/api/npm/npmjs/
